From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qdsp6: q6apm-dai: no BATCH flag in push-pull mode

q6apm_dai_hardware_playback and _capture both set SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH
unconditionally. The flag says the hardware position is only known to a
period, which is true of the shared memory endpoints: q6apm_dai_pointer()
returns

	q6apm_get_hw_pointer(prtd->graph, substream->stream) *
	runtime->period_size

In push-pull mode it is not true. The DSP publishes a sample accurate
position in a shared memory buffer and q6apm_dai_pointer() reads the
frame counter and index out of it, which is why the driver already
carries q6apm_push_pull_config(), q6apm_register_watermark_event() and
the pos_buffer. The graph knows which mode it is in before the hardware
descriptor is copied, so the flag can be cleared where it does not hold.

It is not a cosmetic flag. A userspace driving the PCM from a timer has
to keep an extra period queued to cover a pointer that only advances in
period steps - PipeWire does exactly this in recalc_headroom(), and so
every stream pays a period of latency and up to a period of jitter, for
a position that in push-pull mode is exact.

No functional change for a topology whose playback graph uses
WR_SHARED_MEM_EP, which is every topology in linux-firmware today.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -462,6 +462,22 @@
 		runtime->hw = q6apm_dai_hardware_playback;
 	else if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE)
 		runtime->hw = q6apm_dai_hardware_capture;
+
+	/*
+	 * SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH means the position is only known to a period.
+	 * That is true of the shared memory endpoints, where q6apm_dai_pointer()
+	 * returns the DSP's buffer index multiplied by the period size, but not
+	 * of push-pull mode, where the DSP publishes a sample accurate position
+	 * in shared memory and the pointer is read from there.
+	 *
+	 * The flag is not free: a userspace that drives the PCM from a timer
+	 * has to keep a whole extra period queued to cover a pointer that only
+	 * moves in period steps, which is a period of added latency and a
+	 * period of jitter on every stream. Clear it where the position is
+	 * exact, so only the graphs that need it pay for it.
+	 */
+	if (q6apm_is_graph_in_push_pull_mode(prtd->graph))
+		runtime->hw.info &= ~SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH;
 
 	/* Ensure that buffer size is a multiple of period size */
 	ret = snd_pcm_hw_constraint_integer(runtime, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_PERIODS);
